WEBVTT

00:01.340 --> 00:05.980
<i>I promise, I will make your dream come true.</i>

00:12.360 --> 00:15.740
<i>It was something that no one 
had ever accomplished...</i>

00:16.270 --> 00:19.140
<i>I was sure I had pulled it off.</i>

00:23.000 --> 00:27.550
<i>Or at least, I thought I had...</i>

00:30.400 --> 00:33.810
<i>I truly feel so helpless.</i>

01:15.550 --> 01:24.310
TONIKAWA

01:15.550 --> 01:24.310
TONIKAWA

02:05.520 --> 02:10.020
<b>Episode 12     In All the Times to Come, And Beyond</b>

02:06.030 --> 02:10.270
There's something that feels great 
about morning in the mountains.

02:10.270 --> 02:12.480
I can feel my soul being cleansed.

02:13.620 --> 02:17.330
And sleeping in a big bed was fantastic.

02:17.920 --> 02:21.300
Next time we move, 
I definitely wanna get one.

02:22.020 --> 02:23.590
You seem to be enjoying yourself.

02:24.570 --> 02:27.120
Tokiko-san? Good morning.

02:27.120 --> 02:28.220
Morning.

02:28.220 --> 02:30.700
Are you out for a morning stroll?

02:30.700 --> 02:31.250
Yep.

02:31.920 --> 02:37.010
We're in the middle of the great outdoors.
It seems wasteful not to get up early.

02:37.410 --> 02:38.850
I agree.

02:38.850 --> 02:43.120
I invited Tsukasa-chan, too, 
but she said it was fine.

02:43.120 --> 02:47.020
Well, nature doesn't really 
interest her that much.

02:47.600 --> 02:50.270
I-I guess you're right.

02:50.690 --> 02:54.180
Care for some coffee, Nasa-kun?

02:54.180 --> 02:55.270
Were you making some?

03:01.170 --> 03:02.530
Nasa-kun?

03:08.800 --> 03:10.210
There you go.

03:10.210 --> 03:13.040
I appreciate it. Thanks for the coffee.

03:17.490 --> 03:20.550
Are you sure you shouldn't go and wake her?

03:21.630 --> 03:22.900
Why do you ask?

03:22.900 --> 03:27.010
I mean, look at all this. 
It's totally a couple thing.

03:28.160 --> 03:32.810
Looking at the early morning view, on a 
beautiful morning, up in the mountains...

03:32.810 --> 03:38.720
That seems like something best suited for a 
lovey-dovey couple, and not a random old lady.

03:38.720 --> 03:41.450
Oh, but I'm having a great time.

03:42.500 --> 03:43.420
Really?

03:45.200 --> 03:47.200
Care for some toast, then?

03:47.680 --> 03:50.270
This is from a good bakery in Ginza.

03:51.170 --> 03:52.210
You don't mind?

03:52.210 --> 03:57.360
I bet the smell will be enough 
to lure her out of bed, too.

03:57.360 --> 03:59.140
She's like a rhinoceros beetle that way.

03:59.140 --> 04:00.710
A beetle?

04:06.540 --> 04:09.470
This multi-roaster does a 
fantastic job with toast.

04:10.180 --> 04:12.970
You brought your own, Tokiko-san?

04:12.970 --> 04:18.690
That's right. I love how compact 
they make camping gear.

04:18.690 --> 04:19.730
I see.

04:20.040 --> 04:23.480
The butter's a really good French brand, too.

04:24.320 --> 04:25.990
That's really something!

04:32.120 --> 04:33.560
This is really good!

04:33.560 --> 04:36.630
Isn't it? You can always tell 
the good stuff from the aroma.

04:41.730 --> 04:44.360
I appreciate you joining me for this.

04:44.980 --> 04:48.510
Oh, it's actually been a lot 
of fun to discover new things.

04:48.780 --> 04:50.220
What new things?

04:50.220 --> 04:53.170
The toast, the butter, the way you made it...

04:53.170 --> 04:55.140
I can tell you're particular 
about the whole process.

04:55.790 --> 04:59.260
That's something that 
reminds me of Tsukasa-chan.

05:02.890 --> 05:05.820
Is that right? I take after her, huh?

05:06.430 --> 05:07.660
Oh, that reminds me.

05:07.970 --> 05:11.540
There was something I wanted 
to talk to you about, Nasa-kun.

05:12.080 --> 05:12.990
Me?

05:12.990 --> 05:13.790
Yes.

05:14.780 --> 05:15.890
I wanted to ask...

05:17.770 --> 05:20.230
I knew I smelled something amazing!

05:20.230 --> 05:22.640
That's the bread from that 
famous bakery in Ginza!

05:22.640 --> 05:25.660
And here's your rhinoceros beetle,
 with her awful timing.

05:25.660 --> 05:27.360
Good morning, Tsukasa-chan.

05:27.360 --> 05:28.890
Good morning, darling.

05:29.230 --> 05:31.890
And you're eating this without me?! No fair!

05:31.890 --> 05:35.720
Oh, please. I'll make you some, if you like.

05:36.220 --> 05:38.520
Really? Two pieces, then.

05:38.880 --> 05:40.200
Good grief...

05:40.990 --> 05:44.610
Tell me, Nasa-kun, are you
 sure about this girl?

05:45.030 --> 05:48.220
Hey! First thing in the morning 
and you want to start with this?!

05:48.220 --> 05:51.250
I'm just saying, as sweet as he is,

05:51.250 --> 05:55.290
Nasa-kun could probably land a girl who's 
less of a mess first thing in the morning.

05:56.160 --> 06:00.980
Oh, no, I don't intend to marry anyone else.

06:02.960 --> 06:05.340
You heard him. Bet you liked that, huh?

06:05.340 --> 06:07.000
Sh-Shut up!

06:20.060 --> 06:22.310
The camping trip was a lot of fun, huh?

06:22.310 --> 06:25.070
It was. Way more than I expected.

06:25.860 --> 06:30.510
I never really understood what the 
point of wedding ceremonies was,

06:30.510 --> 06:32.450
but it's probably a lot like that.

06:32.450 --> 06:33.700
Like what?

06:34.540 --> 06:36.700
Having everyone affirm your 
happiness like that...

06:37.290 --> 06:38.960
A lot of things can happen in life,

06:39.350 --> 06:44.210
but on a day like that, everyone
 is just focusing on being happy.

06:44.690 --> 06:46.700
That's the kind of event it is.

06:47.730 --> 06:49.170
That makes sense.

06:49.170 --> 06:50.590
Not only that...

06:51.220 --> 06:54.470
Even if it was only a veil,
 you looked really cute.

06:54.730 --> 06:58.820
W-Well... thanks for that.

07:02.470 --> 07:06.610
There was something I wanted 
to talk to you about, Nasa-kun.

07:07.380 --> 07:09.260
<i>I wonder what she was going to ask...</i>

07:11.360 --> 07:13.370
<b>Call</b>

07:11.360 --> 07:13.370
<b>Kijima (Landlord)</b>

07:11.680 --> 07:13.370
Hey, it's the landlord.

07:13.370 --> 07:14.830
Landlord?

07:14.830 --> 07:15.860
Hello?

07:17.160 --> 07:19.160
Understood. Thanks.

07:20.360 --> 07:21.370
What was that about?

07:22.460 --> 07:24.630
The apartment building is almost finished.

07:25.430 --> 07:26.630
What apartment building?

07:27.240 --> 07:30.260
They're almost done rebuilding 
my old place that burned down.

07:31.360 --> 07:34.570
You mean we won't be staying 
here for free much longer?

07:34.570 --> 07:36.230
It looks that way.

07:36.230 --> 07:39.290
We should be able to move in fairly soon.

07:41.580 --> 07:43.690
I'm kind of nervous.

07:43.690 --> 07:44.520
About what?

07:45.150 --> 07:49.280
It'll be just the two of us 
for real at that point.

07:51.740 --> 07:53.280
Well, yes, it would...

07:53.280 --> 07:54.870
Y-Yeah.

07:55.360 --> 07:59.000
S-Since it's almost ready, 
wanna check the building out?

08:00.080 --> 08:03.040
O-Oh, that's a good idea!

08:07.810 --> 08:10.000
Well, that's impressive.

08:10.000 --> 08:11.550
Very fancy.

08:11.830 --> 08:14.120
And bigger, I think?

08:14.120 --> 08:17.300
I heard they bought some of the surrounding 
properties when they rebuilt it.

08:17.300 --> 08:19.660
And... well...

08:20.890 --> 08:23.650
The apartments... have bathtubs, apparently.

08:24.640 --> 08:26.680
That sounds conven...ient.

08:27.820 --> 08:30.010
W-Well, isn't that something?!

08:30.010 --> 08:31.890
Huh, fancy that.

08:31.890 --> 08:33.200
Y-Yeah...

08:33.200 --> 08:37.200
W-Would we be buying a b-bed, too?

08:37.470 --> 08:38.760
Y-Yeah.

08:39.520 --> 08:42.620
Probably a double bed.

08:43.220 --> 08:46.780
M-Makes sense. That'd be the thing to do.

08:46.780 --> 08:48.210
Y-Yep.

08:48.460 --> 08:51.150
Now I'm nervous, too.

08:51.150 --> 08:51.820
Yeah.

08:53.120 --> 08:54.840
But I'm looking forward to it!

08:55.800 --> 08:56.470
To what?

08:57.580 --> 08:59.970
T-To what? Well... y'know!

09:01.390 --> 09:05.740
So, if we're going to move out, 
we need to organize things here.

09:05.740 --> 09:08.320
We don't actually have 
that much stuff, I think.

09:08.320 --> 09:11.500
Well, we moved in after everything 
burned up at the old place.

09:12.340 --> 09:13.860
There's also...

09:17.100 --> 09:18.990
Senpai!

09:19.380 --> 09:20.550
K-Kaname-chan?

09:20.550 --> 09:22.330
Senpai, you horndog!

09:22.330 --> 09:24.810
Are you serious about moving out?!

09:24.810 --> 09:26.500
Well, yeah...

09:26.500 --> 09:30.500
Senpai, you pervert! Do you have some 
sort of problem with this place?!

09:30.500 --> 09:32.930
Not really, no.

09:32.930 --> 09:36.130
And why are your questions and 
insults totally disconnected?

09:37.070 --> 09:41.260
We've just been borrowing this room, 
so it's not like we can stay here indefinitely.

09:41.520 --> 09:46.510
You say that, but I bet it's just because 
you can't fool around like you want to.

09:47.260 --> 09:52.200
You and Tsukassan both seem like you're 
not particular about where you live!

09:52.200 --> 09:54.780
I'm gonna be lonely if 
you two just disappear!

09:54.780 --> 09:56.030
But still...

09:56.030 --> 09:59.450
I promise to pretend I didn't see 
anything when you fool around at night!

09:59.450 --> 10:01.240
But still!

10:01.240 --> 10:02.530
It's okay.

10:02.970 --> 10:05.590
You won't get a chance to be that lonely.

10:05.590 --> 10:06.540
Tsukassan?

10:06.860 --> 10:11.540
Even when we move out, I'll still be working 
at the bathhouse, so I'll be here all the time.

10:11.830 --> 10:13.520
R-Really?!

10:13.520 --> 10:16.520
Yeah. I enjoy working the front desk.

10:16.520 --> 10:19.440
And I'd miss you, too.

10:19.440 --> 10:22.110
If you're not going to do 
anything with this room,

10:22.110 --> 10:25.310
I think Nasa-kun could work here.

10:25.310 --> 10:28.940
All I really need is my computer. 
I can work just about anywhere.

10:29.400 --> 10:33.360
So, seriously, you don't need to feel bad.

10:33.360 --> 10:36.200
I'd miss you just as much as you'd miss me.

10:37.070 --> 10:38.840
Thanks for having us, Kaname.

10:39.460 --> 10:45.050
Well, in that case... I guess I can put up 
with not getting to peek in on you at night.

10:45.050 --> 10:45.700
Hang on!

10:46.130 --> 10:48.990
You weren't actually peeking 
in on us before now, right?

10:57.760 --> 11:01.970
It was fun and lively staying 
at Kaname-chan's house,

11:02.260 --> 11:05.070
but I'm still really looking 
forward to our new place.

11:05.070 --> 11:06.380
How's that?

11:06.380 --> 11:08.890
Well, it's like...

11:09.620 --> 11:12.230
We're getting closer to being 
a real husband and wife.

11:12.720 --> 11:15.470
What does being "real" even mean?

11:15.470 --> 11:17.610
A real husband and wife...

11:20.290 --> 11:21.740
can do things like this.

11:26.350 --> 11:27.660
Darling...

11:28.160 --> 11:29.020
Yes?

11:29.020 --> 11:30.720
Well, it's just...

11:32.100 --> 11:33.380
What's wrong?

11:34.620 --> 11:39.960
Since we're married, we should be able to talk 
to each other about what's on our minds, right?

11:39.960 --> 11:42.130
Huh? Y-Yeah, of course.

11:42.130 --> 11:46.500
Which is why I want you to hear me out,
 and not take it personally.

11:48.170 --> 11:50.580
Promise you won't get mad?

11:50.580 --> 11:52.890
I-I would never!

11:53.360 --> 11:56.520
Well, to be honest, darling...

11:56.520 --> 11:57.900
Your hugs are crappy!

11:57.900 --> 12:02.000
<i>Crappy! Crappy! Crappy! Crappy!</i>

11:59.380 --> 12:02.000
<i>My hugs are crappy?!</i>

12:05.800 --> 12:08.410
Don't be so obviously depressed!

12:08.830 --> 12:10.650
Listen to me, darling.

12:10.650 --> 12:14.840
You're hugging girls the wrong way.

12:16.160 --> 12:17.670
Like just now...

12:17.730 --> 12:25.050
<b>Tsukasa-chan's
 Hugging Lecture</b>

12:17.730 --> 12:25.050
<b>Class Duty:
 Tsukasa/Nasa</b>

12:17.730 --> 12:25.050
<b>Lifting Graph</b>

12:17.730 --> 12:25.050
<b>Arms</b>

12:17.960 --> 12:23.810
You tend to hug by putting 
your arms under mine, right?

12:23.810 --> 12:25.050
Y-Yeah.

12:25.310 --> 12:30.500
But the truth is, that's not very 
comfortable for shorter girls.

12:31.730 --> 12:36.460
This is the kind of position it puts them in!

12:37.030 --> 12:39.670
It feels like like when you pick up a cat!

12:37.310 --> 12:44.570
<b>Form changing based on container=
Are cats actually liquid?</b>

12:39.670 --> 12:41.270
I-I see.

12:41.270 --> 12:44.000
So, come over here, darling.

12:44.000 --> 12:44.570
Okay.

12:44.570 --> 12:46.070
Do it like this...

12:46.070 --> 12:47.390
With your arms up here.

12:53.160 --> 12:56.460
Hey, you're right! This is a much better fit!

12:56.460 --> 13:00.630
Right? And if you do it 
like this, then I can...

13:01.950 --> 13:05.260
Wow, you're really pulling me in!

13:08.480 --> 13:12.300
D-Do you understand how to 
hug girls properly now?

13:12.300 --> 13:14.230
Y-Yes! Understood!

13:15.120 --> 13:16.600
Do you have anything?

13:16.600 --> 13:17.230
Huh?

13:17.230 --> 13:20.090
Things you want to talk to me about.

13:21.960 --> 13:24.500
Let's see... um...

13:25.200 --> 13:26.110
I think a lot, maybe?

13:26.960 --> 13:28.930
Really?! L-Like what?

13:28.930 --> 13:29.740
Well...

13:30.200 --> 13:31.740
The first thing is...

13:32.000 --> 13:34.040
Can I touch you when you're sleeping?

13:34.650 --> 13:35.250
Huh?

13:35.520 --> 13:37.390
No, wait, not like that!

13:37.390 --> 13:40.750
I don't want to mess with 
you while you're sleeping!

13:40.750 --> 13:44.380
Well, I do, but that's not what this is about!

13:44.720 --> 13:47.130
I mean, you're a messy sleeper, right?

13:48.570 --> 13:51.380
So you end up rolling around all over,

13:51.380 --> 13:54.890
and you look cold sometimes, y'know?
Like, your belly gets exposed, for example.

13:55.460 --> 13:59.110
So when that happens, is it okay 
if I put you back under the futon,

13:59.110 --> 14:01.270
or adjust your pajamas? That sort of thing.

14:02.080 --> 14:02.900
No.

14:03.360 --> 14:05.300
Because I'm not a messy sleeper!

14:06.040 --> 14:09.030
Huh?! No, no, you are!

14:09.030 --> 14:12.530
I am not! You just made that up, darling!

14:12.530 --> 14:15.090
What?! Come on, you have to admit it!

14:15.090 --> 14:17.680
I will not! Because it's not true!

14:30.480 --> 14:31.900
Two more years.

14:32.890 --> 14:35.060
That's how much more of my time you can have.

14:35.950 --> 14:37.310
Wh-What is this?

14:37.720 --> 14:39.310
I've found my destiny.

14:39.310 --> 14:40.480
Destiny?

14:40.480 --> 14:44.320
Right. Which is why I want you to 
promise me that after these two years...

14:44.950 --> 14:48.070
You'll stop living for my sake.

14:49.650 --> 14:51.880
You need to live your own life.

14:52.320 --> 14:55.790
Because people's lives 
are fleeting and short.

14:57.770 --> 15:02.010
<i>I know that you're the 
kindest person there is.</i>

15:03.080 --> 15:06.840
<i>And that's why I... why we...</i>

15:07.080 --> 15:09.840
<i>wanted to make your wish come true.</i>

15:10.720 --> 15:14.090
<i>So I really feel so useless.</i>

15:31.160 --> 15:34.860
<i>She'd probably be mad if 
I took a picture of this.</i>

15:38.120 --> 15:40.120
<b>Call</b>

15:38.120 --> 15:40.120
<b>Chitose</b>

15:40.430 --> 15:43.540
Tsukasa-chan, your phone's ringing.

15:46.490 --> 15:49.130
Who the heck is calling so early?

15:49.130 --> 15:50.760
<b>Call</b>

15:49.130 --> 15:50.760
<b>Chitose</b>

15:50.070 --> 15:50.760
Chitose?

15:52.320 --> 15:56.510
Hello? What's up? It's only seven in the morning.

15:58.690 --> 15:59.890
Tokiko <i>what</i>?

16:02.470 --> 16:03.400
Tokiko!

16:07.090 --> 16:08.150
Want a donut?

16:10.640 --> 16:12.650
Not a half-eaten one, no!

16:13.210 --> 16:16.960
And I heard you collapsed! I was worried.

16:16.960 --> 16:20.160
You were worried? Why, thank you.

16:20.160 --> 16:23.540
Um... Are you feeling all right?

16:24.540 --> 16:28.670
I'm just fine. Chitose and the 
girls made too much of a fuss.

16:29.320 --> 16:32.480
I get a little dizzy and they 
decide to hospitalize me.

16:32.480 --> 16:34.930
Give us old folks a little credit, you know?

16:35.230 --> 16:39.350
You sure this isn't from you overdoing 
it with that trip to the mountains?

16:39.350 --> 16:42.930
I hate to break it to you, 
but I wasn't overdoing it.

16:42.930 --> 16:46.420
That being the case, no need to worry.

16:46.420 --> 16:48.880
I'll be discharged by tomorrow.

16:47.010 --> 16:48.880
Hey! Where do you think you're going?

16:48.880 --> 16:50.300
Stay in bed!

16:50.300 --> 16:52.080
Just to the bathroom, all right?

16:52.080 --> 16:56.280
And while I'm at it, I'm going to 
talk to my doctor, and grab a coffee.

16:56.730 --> 16:58.800
Grind some levels for me while I'm gone.

16:58.800 --> 16:59.600
Huh?!

16:59.600 --> 17:01.480
H-Hey, hang on!

17:01.480 --> 17:04.410
I know you're not great at it, 
but try not to die too much.

17:04.900 --> 17:06.930
See you in a few, then.

17:12.880 --> 17:16.050
I think I'll go with her.

17:17.760 --> 17:20.700
Whoa, hang on! Darling?

17:27.740 --> 17:28.490
Hey...

17:29.410 --> 17:32.320
Are you really okay?

17:32.550 --> 17:35.540
Oh, dear, you found me already, huh?

17:35.540 --> 17:37.820
How'd you figure it out?

17:37.820 --> 17:39.680
Just a feeling?

17:39.680 --> 17:40.490
Not that.

17:41.280 --> 17:42.350
It's your stride.

17:43.640 --> 17:47.580
Compared to when you were in the 
mountains, it's a lot smaller.

17:48.010 --> 17:51.240
That made me think something 
might really be wrong.

17:52.090 --> 17:54.870
You are quite impressive, you know that?

17:55.340 --> 17:56.220
Not really.

17:56.660 --> 18:00.320
People have made a fuss about how great I am,

18:00.320 --> 18:02.470
but I suppose this shows 
there's always someone better.

18:02.470 --> 18:03.720
I don't think it's like that.

18:04.150 --> 18:07.120
Besides, Tsukasa-chan is the 
one who's really impressive.

18:08.520 --> 18:10.530
No, she's normal.

18:11.230 --> 18:12.980
She is normal.

18:12.980 --> 18:17.240
A totally normal girl, 
with no exceptional talents.

18:17.470 --> 18:20.990
Which is why I can imagine 
it must be a lot of trouble.

18:22.210 --> 18:26.280
That said, I'd appreciate you not 
telling her about my condition.

18:26.750 --> 18:28.110
Oh, okay.

18:28.560 --> 18:33.430
You saw how worried she was 
after hearing I collapsed.

18:33.430 --> 18:35.660
Honestly, give me a break here.

18:36.230 --> 18:37.010
Um...

18:38.280 --> 18:42.140
There was something you wanted to tell 
me at the campground. What was it?

18:43.690 --> 18:45.270
Oh, you remembered that?

18:45.560 --> 18:48.940
Yes. It sounded pretty important.

18:51.520 --> 18:54.960
Seeing how sharp you can be at times...

18:54.960 --> 18:59.720
I'm as relieved as I am jealous. 
It's quite the mix of emotions.

19:01.770 --> 19:02.780
Upsy-daisy.

19:06.880 --> 19:10.790
There was something I spent 
my entire life trying to do.

19:11.110 --> 19:15.040
And it looks like my part in it 
ended before it came to fruition.

19:15.670 --> 19:18.550
I like to think I was almost there, but...

19:18.550 --> 19:20.880
It's quite frustrating, all the same.

19:21.870 --> 19:26.260
But since I tried my best, 
even though I failed,

19:26.260 --> 19:27.810
I don't regret it.

19:28.520 --> 19:31.740
Which is why this is for you.

19:34.320 --> 19:36.320
Whoa... whoa, whoa, whoa!

19:36.670 --> 19:38.480
Tokiko-san, this is—

19:38.480 --> 19:39.690
Just a rock.

19:40.870 --> 19:44.480
A regular old stone, with no
 magic powers or anything.

19:45.770 --> 19:51.710
But the thing is, it took a millennia 
of human effort to collect that stone.

19:51.960 --> 19:58.410
You could say that, after a thousand years, 
it amounted to, "Yeah, it's just a rock."

19:58.410 --> 20:00.470
That's how it goes sometimes.

20:01.320 --> 20:02.720
Nasa-kun...

20:03.600 --> 20:07.220
Please make her happy.

20:08.770 --> 20:13.340
<i>I didn't know what she meant at the time.</i>

20:13.980 --> 20:17.130
<i>But... it felt like she was 
entrusting me with something</i>

20:17.130 --> 20:19.740
<i>even more important than the 
moon rock she handed me.</i>

20:22.070 --> 20:24.110
Yes. You can leave it to me.

20:24.600 --> 20:28.120
I promise to make Tsukasa-chan happy!

20:30.320 --> 20:35.110
Well, I'm feeling a bit better 
with that off my shoulders.

20:35.900 --> 20:37.700
Come on, Nasa-kun, let's head—

20:37.700 --> 20:39.900
Hey! There you are!

20:39.900 --> 20:43.960
Well, you had good timing for once.

20:43.960 --> 20:45.260
What's that supposed to mean?!

20:45.680 --> 20:49.510
And why is this game so ludicrously hard?!

20:50.400 --> 20:54.120
For someone who likes video games so much,
 you never get any better at them.

20:54.120 --> 20:55.680
E-Excuse me?!

20:55.680 --> 20:58.350
Anyway, put down the video game.

20:58.350 --> 20:59.770
The weather's nice,

21:00.540 --> 21:03.400
so go have a nice little 
chat with your husband.

21:03.400 --> 21:05.750
You told me to play the damn thing!

21:06.250 --> 21:09.080
And the fact that you snuck out here...

21:09.080 --> 21:11.280
What were you talking about, anyway?

21:11.280 --> 21:13.030
That's a secret.

21:14.220 --> 21:15.920
Right, Nasa-kun?

21:17.330 --> 21:20.380
Well, I wouldn't say it's that big a deal.

21:20.380 --> 21:23.920
You were probably filling his head 
with more nonsense, weren't you?

21:23.920 --> 21:26.240
You make me sound so awful.

21:26.240 --> 21:31.430
If you're that desperate to find out, 
try paying closer attention to Nasa-kun.

21:31.430 --> 21:32.930
What do you mean by—

21:32.930 --> 21:34.180
I mean...

21:41.280 --> 21:43.130
exactly what I said.

21:46.220 --> 21:48.950
W-Well, to be honest...

21:51.450 --> 21:54.950
I told her about how I 
want to make you happy.

21:55.280 --> 21:57.110
O-Okay.

21:59.150 --> 22:01.210
That's... well...

22:01.450 --> 22:03.460
Um... er...

22:04.070 --> 22:06.220
Th-Thank you.

22:10.300 --> 22:13.770
<b>Closed for the Day</b>

22:10.300 --> 22:13.770
<b>Sorry!</b>
